Act as a world-class front-end design engineer and art director.

I'm replacing my old, vibe-coded portfolio at ekizior.github.io with a lightweight, hyper-clean, single-page site built from scratch in Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Lucide React. This is a teardown and rebuild, not a restyle. Keep nothing from the old codebase unless I say so. The only things carried over are my headshot and the images for my three featured projects.

### 1. Aesthetic Direction (developer minimalism, text-editor portfolios)
- Style: A sleek personal developer index. Compact, very legible, content first.
- Typography: Geist Sans for body text. Geist Mono for metadata, dates, tags, and code-style accents. Load both through `next/font` so they're self-hosted, with no external font requests.
- Palette (dark only, no theme toggle):
  - Background `#121212`
  - Body text `#A1A1AA`
  - Headings and names `#EDEDED`
  - Borders and dividers `#27272A`
  - Everything must meet WCAG AA contrast.
- Layout: One centered column (max-width ~680px) with generous vertical whitespace. Flat design, no clutter.
- Images: Only my headshot and the featured project images. Show them flat, with a 1px `#27272A` border, slightly rounded corners, and no shadows, filters, or overlays. Keep pixel art crisp (`image-rendering: pixelated`).
- Icons: Links are text, not brand logos. Use Lucide only for tiny utility glyphs, such as `ArrowUpRight` on external links.

### 2. Content & Layout Structure
Use exactly these sections, in this order:
1. **Header**: A small circular headshot (~88px) beside the name, one-liner, and location. Then inline text links (GitHub, LinkedIn, Email) whose underline fades in on hover. No resume link, and no downloadable resume anywhere on the site.
2. **About**: One short, conversational paragraph.
3. **Experience**: A chronological ledger. Each row has Role · Company on the left and years in mono, right-aligned. Put a 1–2 sentence impact line under each row.
4. **Featured Projects**: My three favorite projects, shown first. Each is a single-column row with a 4:3 image on the left (stacked above the text on mobile), then the title (linked if there's a URL), year in mono on the right, one sentence, and tech tags.
5. **More Projects**: The remaining projects as a minimalist single-column list, not cards, with no images. Each item has a title (linked if there's a URL), year in mono on the right, one sentence, and tech tags.
   - Tech tags in both project sections are tiny mono pills (`text-xs`, 1px border in `#27272A`, no fill).
6. **Education**: Two compact rows in the same ledger style as Experience.
7. **Footer**: Copyright, a "last updated" date, and a friendly sign-off.

### 3. Absolute Banned List (AI tropes to avoid)
- NO purple or blue glowing gradients, neon accents, or mesh backdrops.
- NO glassmorphism, `backdrop-blur`, or floating translucent cards.
- NO 3-column feature grids or marketing-style cards.
- NO 3D graphics, decorative illustrations, particle canvases, or cursor effects. Project screenshots and artwork in Featured Projects are fine.
- NO entry or scroll animations. The only transitions allowed are 150ms opacity or color changes on hover. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- NO boilerplate copy. Render the text in Section 5 exactly as written. Don't add stats, adjectives, or claims.
- NO skill bars, percentage meters, or logo walls.

### 4. Rebuild & Cleanup Requirements
- **Hosting**: GitHub Pages at `ekizior.github.io` (user site, no `basePath`).
  - Use static export: `output: 'export'`, `images: { unoptimized: true }`, `trailingSlash: true`.
  - Add `public/.nojekyll`.
  - Add a GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) that builds and deploys `out/` with `actions/upload-pages-artifact` and `actions/deploy-pages`.
- **Dependencies**: Only `next`, `react`, `react-dom`, `tailwindcss` (v4, with `@tailwindcss/postcss`), `lucide-react`, TypeScript, and the required types. No animation libraries, UI kits, CMS, analytics, or icon packs.
- **Architecture**:
  - Server Components only. No `"use client"`, since nothing on the page needs it.
  - All copy and image references live in one typed file, `content.ts`. Components only render that data, so future updates touch one file. A project is featured if it has an `image`. Images are static imports from `public/images/`, so Next knows their dimensions.
  - Files: `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, `app/icon.svg`, `content.ts`, and at most 4 small components (`Section`, `LedgerRow`, `Tag`, `FeaturedProject`). Aim for under ~300 lines of app code, not counting `content.ts`.
  - Resize images before committing them: the headshot is ~320px and project images are at most ~1000px on the long side. Every image needs meaningful `alt` text.
- **Semantics & accessibility**:
  - Use `<header>`, `<main>`, `<section>` with `aria-labelledby`, `<footer>`, and real `<ul>` / `<li>` lists.
  - Use `<time>` for dates.
  - Give every interactive element a visible `:focus-visible` style.
  - External links get `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- **Metadata**: Title, description, Open Graph tags, and a simple favicon (monogram "EK" or a plain square, nothing illustrative).
- **Cleanup**: Delete these leftovers from the old site: `src/`, `public/assets/`, `public/favicon.ico`, `.eslintrc.json`, `tailwind.config.ts`, and `README.md`. Keep `public/images/`. Once `src/` is gone, `"src"` can come out of the `tsconfig.json` `exclude` list.

